course: dictionary
lesson: 13285
title: Slow and steady change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some changes happen all at once, and some happen bit by bit. Gradual describes the slow kind, where something changes little by little over time, not suddenly. «The leaves turned brown through a gradual change as autumn arrived.» Nobody saw the leaves change in one moment; the change came over many days.
explain: Gradual can also describe a slope. «The path up the hill has a gradual slope, so the walk is easy.» A gradual slope rises or falls gently, not steeply. Ask yourself: is the change slow and steady, or sudden and sharp? If it is slow and steady, gradual fits.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Her reading got better through gradual improvement.» If you put slow and steady in place of gradual, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Sudden would not fit, because sudden means all at once.
fact: Gradual means happening slowly and little by little over time.
fact: «A gradual increase in temperature» means the temperature rises a bit at a time, not in one jump.
fact: In maths, a gradual slope is gentle, not steep.
fact: Gradual is the opposite of sudden.
fact: Other phrases you may meet: gradual change, gradual improvement, gradual growth.
exercise: «The river wore away the rock through gradual erosion over thousands of years.» What does gradual mean here? | Very fast and sudden | Made of stone | *Slow and little by little | Wet and muddy
exercise: «The road climbed the hill on a gradual slope, so the cyclists could pedal easily.» What is a gradual slope? | A steep wall | A hole in the ground | A flat floor with no hills | *A gentle slope that rises slowly
exercise: «Sam's reading got better through gradual improvement, one page at a time.» Which word means the opposite of gradual? | Steady | *Sudden | Slow | Little by little
test: «The temperature had a gradual increase during the morning, rising a little each hour.» What does gradual increase suggest? | A sudden jump in one moment | A big storm | *A rise that happens slowly over time | A fall in temperature
test: Which phrase describes a slope you can walk up easily? | A steep cliff | A sudden drop | *A gradual slope | A jump over a wall
exam: Mia says gradual means fast, because it sounds like grad. Is she right? | Yes, it means the same as sudden | Yes, gradual means quick and sudden | *No, gradual means slow and little by little | No, gradual means very loud
